From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Sun, 14 Jun 2026 08:16:17 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 01755/11362] [outer-loop] spec the verifier-as-DETECTOR
 measurement (operator-chosen next direction, cheap)

Isolates the verifier's DETECTION value (flag/reject wrong outputs -> AUROC, abstention
curve) from its SELECTION value (oracle@K-vote, headroom-conditional). Detection has value
even where selection headroom is ~0 (Sudoku). Uses cached data only (TRM snapshots +
executable verifier; .387/.388 cached pools). Guardrails: AUROC>0.5 CI95, valid-but-wrong
hard split (not just trivial invalid-grid detection), decoding sanity-check, substrate
honesty. Does NOT move the DiffusionGemma gate (that's selection/guidance).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
